      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral\nargument before the Supreme Court of the United States at\n11:16 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "IRVING L. GORNSTEIN, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor\nGeneral, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on\nbehalf of the United States, as amicus curiae\nsupporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner comes before the Court asking one\nthing and one thing only, that the State of California be\nbound by its decrees and its laws that have guided it\nthroughout the history of California, that the State and\nthe Federal Government be bound by the laws of the land\nthat have been in place essentially since the State's\nfoundation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Did he base his decision, the one\nthat you're referring to, on the Ex Post Facto Clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: So did the Frazer case overrule some of this California doctrine on statute of limitations that you've just told us about?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF JANET GAARD ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Gaard",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "extended the statute of limitations for the most serious of these offenses and it expressly made the law retroactive. This law does not violate the Ex Post Facto Clause or the Due Process Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the Ex Post Facto Clause has been interpreted in terms of the four Calder categories."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0002-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF IRVING L. GORNSTEIN ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES AS AMICUS CURIAE SUPPORTING THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "California's statute of limitations does not violate the Ex Post Facto Clause because it does not violate any of the four Calder categories."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roberto Najera (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b513751abf71770902c71e6e4f5651fb7d720ac1811d0e51689632943ef81cfc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b513751abf71-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would ask, as I said in the beginning, that this Court hold the State to the bargain that it chose to make, to the terms that it chose to define by creating the statute of limitations."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
